function.arguments:
{"ok": true, "summary": "Cause: the dynamic build's Class::plain_set (the per-class cached "is this a plain store" gate) only tracked __setattr__/__frozen__ hooks and properties. __slots__ was kept as an ordinary class attribute but never enforced, so any instance attribute could be set and __dict__ was always materialized.

Change: set_info now also caches an Option<SlotSet> (has_dict + the slot names collected from the MRO, computed once per class per epoch). plain_set returns false for non-storable names, and the slow paths of setattr (after prop/__setattr__/__frozen__ handling) and object_setattr raise CPython's exact AttributeError ("'S' object has no attribute 'b' and no __dict__ for setting new attributes") when the name is no slot and there is no __dict__. getattr and object.__getattribute__ only return a live __dict__ when the class has one (own body without __slots__, or "__dict__" listed in it); otherwise the read raises CPython's message, so hasattr(obj, "__dict__") agrees. A string __slots__ is one name; tuple/list/dict forms work; slots inherit and a subclass without __slots__ gets a __dict__ again. A class with no __slots__ anywhere in its MRO pays only one cached Option tag check per assignment on the fast path.

Tested: run_check passes (slots.py normal + BREVI_DYN=1 output identical to python3, 40/40 guard programs still typed); added tests/dyn/slots_enforced.py + .expected (verified byte-identical output across CPython, brevi normal and BREVI_DYN=1) and changelog.d/dyn-slots.md; probed nearby cases (inheritance, empty slots, "__dict__"/"__weakref__" in slots, list/dict/string slots, class-attribute shadowing, custom __setattr__ via object/super.__setattr__, pydantic-style __pydantic_* storage). Perf: 20M assignments on a plain class, 3 rounds each — before: normal 1.177s, dynamic 1.026s (min); after: normal 1.448s, dynamic 1.565s (min), but the after-session's CPython control ran 2.8–3.2s vs 2.2–2.5s in the before-session, so session noise dominates; the added per-assignment work is a single predictable cached-flag check."}
